# e18_drift.gbnf: the two literals of rust/src/rules.rs, letter for letter, in the
# house shape extended by one key. The "decision" key keeps the house name so that
# tools/agreement.py reads it unchanged, and the "summary" key holds one sentence of
# 10 to 160 characters that ends in a full stop, so the end of generation token is
# reachable only after a complete sentence. The class admits no quote, no brace and
# no newline, so the object always closes and the log's CSV quoting stays simple.
# NOMINAL is first because the stub answers the first literal on every path, in CI
# and in the Rust stub of rust/src/abi.rs, which must agree byte for byte with
# common/c/src/edgellm_stub.c on this grammar: {"decision":"NOMINAL","summary":"."}.
# ws admits spaces and tabs only, never a newline.
root ::= "{" ws "\"decision\"" ws ":" ws decision ws "," ws "\"summary\"" ws ":" ws summary ws "}"
decision ::= "\"NOMINAL\"" | "\"DRIFT\""
summary ::= "\"" [A-Za-z0-9 ,.%]{9,159} "." "\""
ws ::= [ \t]*
